      "math_academy_id": "q-159350",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [0,2],$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}y}{2}.\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{X}(x),$ the marginal CDF of $X,$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=F(x,\\infty )={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le x\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & =F(x,\\infty ) \\\\  & =F(x,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(2)}{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
